# requirements/stellar/cluster-search.ears
capability: Stellar cluster search
owner: stellar
requirements:
  - id: STL-001
    pattern: event
    text: "When target regions are predeclared, the system shall record the reason for each region."
    rationale: "Region choice is a researcher degree of freedom; it must be declared."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    gates: [STL-G-01]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_every_predeclared_region_carries_its_reason_and_an_empty_one_is_refused"
  - id: STL-002
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall apply feature-space transformations as versioned policies and keep raw five-axis Euclidean clustering out of every gate."
    rationale: "Five raw Euclidean axes mix incommensurate units."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_clustering_takes_only_a_feature_matrix_from_a_registered_policy"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_rescaling_proper_motion_units_leaves_the_feature_matrix_unchanged"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_a_small_rigid_rotation_of_the_field_leaves_memberships_unchanged"
  - id: STL-003
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall take quality cuts from configuration recorded in the manifest."
    rationale: "Quality cuts change results; they are configuration, not code."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_quality_cuts_report_what_each_cut_removed"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_the_quality_cuts_and_their_effect_are_in_the_manifest"
  - id: STL-004
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where a GPU clustering adapter is used, the system shall exclude its results from gates unless the agreement test passed in the same release."
    rationale: "GPU results are admissible only after agreement with the CPU reference (ADR-007)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    gates: [STL-G-08]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_clustering::test_agreement_passes_only_when_labels_and_memberships_match_the_cpu_reference"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_gpu_results_reach_the_gates_only_after_agreement"
  - id: STL-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall cross-match a candidate against two benchmarks before it labels the candidate potentially new."
    rationale: "A candidate that matches a known cluster is not new."
    verification: test
    tiers: []
    gates: [STL-G-06]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_without_a_second_benchmark_nothing_is_called_potentially_new"
  - id: STL-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall run null-field and injection tests per region with recorded seeds."
    rationale: "False-positive and completeness estimates need reproducible seeds."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_null_fields_are_seeded_and_destroy_the_planted_kinematics"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_components::test_injection_is_seeded_and_scored_by_best_overlap"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_null_and_injection_runs_cover_every_region_with_recorded_seeds"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_the_same_seed_reproduces_the_findings"
  - id: STL-007
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall retain rejected and inconclusive candidates with their failure reasons."
    rationale: "Negative results are evidence."
    verification: test
    tiers: []
    gates: [STL-G-07]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_rejected_candidates_are_retained_with_their_reasons"
  - id: STL-008
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall take the candidate pass marks for member count, stability across the grid, CMD coherence and the largest allowed share of the searched stars from the predeclaration's parameters."
    rationale: "The pass marks decide which candidates reach the cross-match; as predeclared parameters they are frozen with the hash, so changing one is a new predeclaration (resolves D15)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_the_pass_marks_are_predeclared_so_changing_one_changes_the_hash_and_the_outcome"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_protocol::test_malformed_pass_marks_are_refused_at_planning_not_coerced"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_the_field_itself_is_rejected_as_most_of_the_stars"
  - id: STL-009
    pattern: event
    text: "When the system sweeps the sky for clusters, the system shall search each tile with the predeclared cuts and pass marks, keep only candidates centred inside the tile, run at least one null field per tile, count each star searched in one tile only, refuse to mix tiles searched over a different prepared catalogue or set of known-cluster catalogues, and label every finding exploratory."
    rationale: "A whole-sky search is not predeclared region by region, so its findings are leads for a predeclared run (sdp discover run), never a verdict; half-open tiles stop a cluster on an edge being counted twice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_every_point_of_the_sky_is_in_exactly_one_tile"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_a_tile_counts_as_searched_only_the_stars_inside_it_not_its_rim"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_discover::test_tiles_are_not_reused_once_the_catalogue_or_the_benchmarks_change"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_a_tile_keeps_only_candidates_centred_inside_it"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_a_planted_cluster_in_no_benchmark_comes_out_potentially_new_and_labelled_exploratory"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_without_a_null_field_a_new_looking_candidate_is_only_inconclusive"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_a_null_field_survivor_makes_new_looking_candidates_inconclusive"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_sweep::test_settings_share_the_predeclared_cuts_and_pass_marks"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_discover::test_prepare_sweep_report_finds_the_planted_cluster_in_no_benchmark"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_discover::test_the_predeclared_run_reads_gaia_and_issues_a_verdict"
  - id: STL-010
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where the settings name the cluster-distance CMD policy, the stellar module shall place every member and every compared field star at the inverse-variance mean parallax of the members before measuring CMD coherence."
    rationale: "A member's own parallax error adds about 0.43 mag of scatter at parallax/error 5, so faint real clusters failed the coherence check; field stars at the cluster's distance are treated the same way so the comparison stays fair. The sweep uses this policy; the UC-01 predeclaration names none and keeps member-parallax."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_a_faint_real_cluster_passes_at_its_distance_where_its_own_parallaxes_blur_it"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_random_field_stars_at_the_same_distance_are_still_no_tighter_than_the_field"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_the_cluster_parallax_is_the_inverse_variance_mean_of_usable_members"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_too_few_field_stars_at_the_cluster_distance_is_inconclusive_not_failed"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_a_cluster_that_dominates_its_distance_is_compared_with_its_nearest_field_stars"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_the_predeclared_run_keeps_member_parallax_and_the_sweep_uses_the_cluster_distance"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_an_unknown_cmd_policy_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_a_small_cluster_in_a_sparse_field_is_compared_with_enough_of_its_nearest_field_stars"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_a_star_clipped_from_the_sequence_is_not_readmitted_by_a_later_fit"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_an_unknown_cmd_policy_is_refused_even_when_the_search_finds_nothing"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_a_sweep_tile_with_an_unknown_cmd_policy_is_refused_before_it_is_skipped"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_cmd_policy::test_the_tile_columns_read_once_give_the_same_coherence_as_reading_them_per_candidate"
  - id: STL-011
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where the settings name a significance test, the stellar module shall reject every candidate whose members' k-th nearest-neighbour distances in the feature space are not smaller than those of the non-members around it at the settings' minimum significance."
    rationale: "A per-candidate significance, after Hunt & Reffert's (2021) cluster significance test, replaces a tile-wide yes or no from one null field: in the sweep a potentially new candidate must also be more significant than every false candidate its tile's null fields produced, so one noisy tile no longer hides a real cluster beside it. The UC-01 predeclaration names no test."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_a_dense_group_is_many_sigma_above_the_stars_around_it"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_a_random_handful_of_the_field_is_not_significant"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_the_significance_is_capped_where_the_p_value_underflows"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_too_few_members_or_surrounding_stars_cannot_be_assessed"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_the_field_sample_is_the_stars_nearest_the_candidate_not_the_whole_tile"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_malformed_significance_settings_are_refused"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_the_predeclared_run_has_no_significance_test_and_the_sweep_has_one"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_the_assessment_refuses_to_run_the_test_without_the_feature_matrix"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_in_the_sweep_the_planted_cluster_is_significant_and_the_field_itself_is_not"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_a_null_survivor_more_significant_than_the_candidate_makes_it_inconclusive"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_significance::test_a_new_candidate_is_held_to_each_false_candidate_of_its_tile"
